{"title":"2014 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The pie chart shows the distribution of the number of bronze, silver and gold medals in a school’s trophy case.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(add image on problem 1 page: 2x degrees for Bronze, 3x degrees for Silver and right angle for Gold)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Write the ratio of the number of bronze medals to the number of silver medals to the number of gold medals in lowest terms.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2014 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 1a\">part a</a>, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1cb5bdce2d06d2419066a2b55ab01d824217bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the angle for the bronze portion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c8a41c4f7db581fe0747f21dcd0b9a44cbb5b48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54 \\times 2 = 2^{2} \\times 3^{3} = 108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" /> and the angle for the silver portion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4277a209f6237b5503518e985f2a9a992e91e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54 \\times 3 = 2 \\times 3^{4} = 162^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The ratio is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5c6aa839e3832d005d5d683e51e2aeff8d638de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108:162:90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" /> if not reduced.\n</p><p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c20629a408724587e05c5d7bf53692a14f81d12d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 = 2 \\times 3^{2} \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Using the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75cef16b301d38a271625130c1aac46a7e9ce72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/911bd1cd1243d0fb147bd1300b1e2f867a86f1eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$162$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we realize that the greatest common factor that all three numbers share is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85762675850d14a6dfbd580d82a40a30d7750fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3^{2} = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Dividing each number by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e443b86825a9a3699bf2a5d3a5c2020a809c9a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265e371ee5b45656271abf625b033a97e8ed01bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^{2} \\times 3^{3}}{2 \\times 3^{2}} = 2 \\times 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"159\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a9fcbefbd1df07bc5d0904d06454efa9e195df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2 \\times 3^{4}}{2 \\times 3^{2}} = 3^{2} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"128\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/caca07cdcaecaea778f95fd78a1bc2534b6a9e0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2 \\times 3^{2} \\times 5}{2 \\times 3^{2}} = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"118\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>From this, we realize that the reduced ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/554e5e299ffc2a800eec102b23f6964082a97b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{6:9:5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"71\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234430\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 61/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 983/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2890/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.394      1 2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   12.394      1 -total\n 42.52%    5.270      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35629:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234430 and revision id 278073. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}